SUMMARY: Against Tech Oligarchy: The Story of Workers’ Resistance - by U
  of T Jackman Humanities Institute
LOCATION:Jackman Humanities Building
DESCRIPTION:More info:
  https://www.humanities.utoronto.ca/events/against-tech-oligarchy\n\nHoste
 d by U of T Jackman Humanities Institute
  (https://www.humanities.utoronto.ca/)\n\nA book talk on Against Tech
  Oligarchy\, an account of the rise of the tech worker movement and the
  industry backlash it provoked. The book traces how tech workers organized
  against their employers over military contracts\, sexism and working
  conditions\, and how Silicon Valley’s labour politics shifted in
  response.
END:VEVENT
