SUMMARY:Civic Meetup #568: Hack the Count: Turning Window Sensors into
  Street Safety Evidence - by Civic Tech Toronto
LOCATION:In person or online (address available to attendees)
DESCRIPTION:More info:
  https://guild.host/events/civic-meetup-568-hack-90ezjp\n\nHosted by Civic
  Tech Toronto (https://civictech.ca/)\n\nThis talk introduces CIVIC
  (Community-centred Infrastructures for Visible and Inclusive Cities)\, an
  urban living lab in London\, Ontario. Residents host low-cost\,
  privacy-by-design Telraam traffic sensors and noise monitors in their own
  windows. These sensors count cars\, cyclists and pedestrians and estimate
  speeds\, all without storing images.
END:VEVENT
